# Source for s1-ghz2-loop.bk2 (InputLogAuthorTool --script). Green Hill Act 2 from its level
# start, derived with GameplayInputBranchTool from s1-complete-run.bk2 (not edited by hand):
#   GameplayInputBranchTool --skip-rows 7094,7283,7746,7796,8110 --input-start 6622 --resume 500
#     <s1 ROM> s1 ghz 2 320 sonic none src/test/resources/traces/s1/_movies/s1-complete-run.bk2
#     1808 <out> '1 R'
# --skip-rows drops the five native lag rows (ghz2_completerun rows 472, 661, 1124, 1174, 1488,
# where the recorded gameplay_frame_counter repeats): VBlank_Lag (sonic.asm:711-712) never reaches
# ReadJoypads, so the native pad was not polled there and a direct boot, which polls every step,
# must not consume them. With them dropped, the unchanged replay matches the trace's positions on
# every row through capture frame 2308. The one change is Right on frame 1808, the frame he lands
# from the loop-side drop (trace row 1813), where the recording held nothing until row 1834; he
# faces and runs right from the landing instead of running backwards. The loop and the rings are
# unchanged (41 rings by frame 2035, as in the recording).
